<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parmehutu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Party of the Hutu Emancipation Movement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parmehutu (Party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> Emancipation Movement) was a Rwandan political party founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregoire-kayibanda">Grégoire Kayibanda</a> in 1959 from his earlier Hutu social movement. It led the Hutu revolution against Tutsi dominance, won the elections before independence and ruled Rwanda as a one-party state from 1962 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juvenal-habyarimana">Juvénal Habyarimana</a>'s coup in 1973.</p></div>
